{"id": "37a60121-5772-4eeb-9817-2482532dfd54", "timestamp": "2026-10-23T01:13:52.217427", "source": "user", "parent_id": "a3bbafc1-2472-4866-9441-6b55ad265c8d", "llm_message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "{"researcher_request": "Approach is largely sound as a *design*; two things before I let you proceed to the full design write-up. Please address both in your Stage=main deliverable; no execution code yet, just paper-design-level detail. **(1) Ground-truth cadence / interpretation: confirm and lock** the strict interpretation: the success criterion is that regenerated torsions reproduce *ground-truth frequency content in the band destroyed by subsampling* (matched against the fine-cadence reference at each torsion's native fs/ps resolution), not just plausible marginal torsions. In your final design, state this explicitly, and pair it with two fallback interpretations (A: matched against ground truth at the *stride* resolution; B: marginals-only / Ramachandran JSD), so the metric battery is interpretable even if MDGEN's emitted frames turn out to be coarse rather than fine. **(2) Path forward:** proceed in the current role — write the full experiment design (rationale, controls, analysis plan, feasibility, risks) as a single self-contained document. Required contents: (a) system choice with explicit justification (alanine dipeptide as primary because cleanest φ/ψ dynamics and fast oscillation visibility; chignolin as secondary in-distribution check); (b) ground-truth source plan — prefer a fine-cadence public trajectory (mdtraj tutorial data or equivalent), with a stated minimum length needed for Welch PSD convergence in the target band; (c) the stride sweep S ∈ {1 ns, 10 ns, 100 ns} at fixed generated length, plus the H1/H0 framing per band; (d) full metric battery in priority order (Welch PSD integrated power in the lost high-frequency band as primary; autocorrelation τ_c; 1D/2D torsion F(φ)/F(ψ) via JSD; MSM/HMM implied timescales with lag-time sweep; Hilbert amplitude & zero-crossing period; cartesian/torsion RMSD as sanity); (e) controls L0 (constant-copy), L1 (linear-interpolation in atoms — the non-negotiable beating baseline), L2 (linear in torsion), L3 (exact subsample passthrough), each explicitly defined by what they can/cannot recover so the ablation is interpretable; (f) statistical design: n ≥ 32 generations per (system, stride, seed) cell with independent seeds, pre-declared CIs on PSD-integrated-power and τ_c; (g) feasibility note — explicitly state this plan targets an out-of-sandbox execution harness with MDGEN repo+weights+mdtraj installed, and that this /workspace cannot run it; (h) pre-registered decision rules: what counts as 'recovers' (e.g., primary metric within ground-truth 95% CI in the lost band, with ablations beating L1 etc.); (i) failure modes (MDGEN emitting coarse frames, topology mismatch on generated structure, insufficient ground-truth length, ambiguity in torsion segmentation deep in chignolin) and mitigations. Keep it as a design document; do not write runnable code, do not invent numeric results. Approve now: continue.", "required_handoff_stage": "result", "approach_approved": true}"}], "tool_calls": null, "tool_call_id": null, "name": null}, "llm_response_id": null, "activated_skills": [], "extended_content": [], "sender": null, "kind": "MessageEvent", "source_event_index": 12}
