l": {"id": "call-cc33e35f-8bb9-4282-80ef-ead603b93c83", "responses_item_id": null, "name": "end_researcher_turn", "arguments": "{"summary": "Deliver full experimental design document", "stage": "result", "answer": "# Experimental Design: Does MDGEN recover fast-timestep torsion-angle dynamics lost in subsampled MD?\n\n---\n\n## 0. Reading of the question (locked)\n\n### 0.1 Primary (strict) reading \u2014 what \"recovers\" must mean\n\n**H1 (recovery)**: For each backbone / side-chain torsion phi, psi, chi tracked at the fine ground-truth cadence dt_truth of order fs to ps, the frequency content of the generated torsion time-series in the spectral band destroyed by subsampling matches that of the ground truth within its 95 percent CI. The destroyed band is formally B_lost(S) = ( f_Nyq(S), f_Nyq(dt_truth) ], where f_Nyq(dt) = 1/(2 dt).\n\n**H0 (no recovery)**: Within B_lost, the generated PSD is statistically indistinguishable from a low-pass signal that cannot exceed f_Nyq(S).\n\nThis is the success criterion. It is a per-dof, per-band frequentist comparison against the original fs/ps trajectory.\n\n### 0.2 Fallback A \u2014 stride-matched comparison\nIf MDGEN's emitted frames have an effective inter-frame interval dt_gen close to or coarser than dt_truth's Nyquist bound, comparison is reduced to aligning both at stride resolution. B_lost becomes effectively empty and the test reduces to \"does MDGEN preserve trends (slowest modes).\" A strictly weaker claim than H1.\n\n### 0.3 Fallback B \u2014 marginals-only\nIf A is infeasible, comparison reduces to 1D F(phi), F(psi), 2D Ramachandran via JSD. Tests whether MDGEN generates plausible torsions, not whether it recovers their time-evolution. Strictly weaker negative or positive.\n\nThe primary/A/B tier is pre-registered; whichever tier's reportable statistic is invoked must be so flagged.\n\n---\n\n## 1. System choice\n\n### 1.1 Primary: alanine dipeptide (Ace-Ala-Nme, neutral termini)\nJustification:\n1. Torsion-only reaction coordinate: phi and psi are the slow, large-amplitude degrees of freedom; dynamics are defined on Ramachandran.\n2. Fast oscillation visibility: harmonic-like librations around C7eq / C7ax basins sit in 0.1-10 ps regime, well above Nyquist of any S of order ns or larger.\n3. Two-state structure giving MSM plateau.\n4. Compute footprint: ~24000 atoms explicit solvent; tractable.\n5. Out-of-distribution for MDGEN by design \u2014 acceptable because we test physical recovery not in-distribution accuracy. Negative here is dispositive for any realistic protein.\n\n### 1.2 Secondary: chignolin\nJustification: in-distribution for MDGEN's training; multiple torsions per residue (phi_i, psi_i, chi_1) giving >=25 d.f.; mu-scale folding transitions. Caveat: deeper-residue torsions may have segmentation ambiguity (see section 7).\n\n---\n\n## 2. Ground-truth source plan\n\n### 2.1 Source preference order\n1. Public fine-cadence alanine dipeptide dataset (mdtraj tutorial suite provides fs-cadence explicit-solvent data; PyEMMA / PLUMED tutorials likewise; document checksum).\n2. DESRES / Anton chignolin at native reporting.\n3. Fallback: fresh local run in execution harness, AMBER ff14SB or OpenFF 2.x + TIP3P, 100 ns at 1 fs stride, HMR if needed.\n\n### 2.2 Minimum length for Welch PSD convergence\nWelch segment length must capture multiple periods of the slowest oscillation of interest. For alanine dipeptide's libration shoulder: T_min ~ 1 ps. Welch segment of 32 ps = 32 cycles. 32 segments gives estimator variance ~ 1/sqrt(32) ~ 18 percent on PSD power. Therefore ground truth length >= 1 ns at fine cadence, preferably >=10 ns for alanine dipeptide and >=100 ns for chignolin (slower dynamics for MSM).\n\n### 2.3 Storage and preprocessing\nStore fine-cadence trajectory at 100 fs (Nyquist-folds to 10 THz, encompassing libration signal). 100 ns at 100 fs stride = ~28 GB, tractable. Pre-declare dt_truth and f_Nyq(dt_truth); signal band defined as <= 5 THz and locked before metric evaluation to avoid HARKing.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Stride sweep\n\nCells: 6 (system x stride). Each cell N_gen = 32 independent generations with distinct MDGEN noise seeds.\n\n| Cell | System | Stride S | Frames | dt_gen (approx) |\n|------|--------|----------|--------|-----------------|\n| 1 | alanine | 1 ns | MDGEN max | ~5 ps |\n| 2 | alanine | 10 ns | same | same |\n| 3 | alanine | 100 ns | same | same |\n| 4 | chignolin | 1 ns | same | same |\n| 5 | chignolin | 10 ns | same | same |\n| 6 | chignolin | 100 ns | same | same |\n\nH1/H0 per band:\n- Preserved (f <= f_Nyq(S)): H1 = generated tracks GT within CI (sanity).\n- Lost (f_Nyq(S) < f <= f_Nyq(dt_truth)): H1 = generated power within GT 95 percent CI. H0 = generated indistinguishable from constant or linear.\n- Noise floor (f > f_Nyq(dt_truth)): power at numerical noise floor (uninterpretable).\n\nPre-registered successes decided only in Lost band.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Metric battery (priority-ordered)\n\n### 4.1 Primary \u2014 Welch PSD integrated power in lost band\nFor each torsion, Welch PSD of GT (segments averaged to 95 percent CI) and Welch PSD of generated at same cadence. metric_1 = integral from f_Nyq(S) to f_Nyq(dt_truth) of |PSD_gen|/|PSD_gt| df, on fixed log-spaced grid (equal per-decade weighting). Reported with bootstrap 95 percent CI over n=32 generations.\n\n### 4.2 Autocorrelation time tau_c\nACF to half-length; exponential fit; relative error |tau_c_gen - tau_c_gt|/tau_c_gt.\n\n### 4.3 Torsion marginals via JSD\n1D F(phi), F(psi): 36 bins of 10 degrees on S^1. 2D Ramachandran: 36x36 grid. JSD in nats.\n\n### 4.4 MSM/HMM implied timescales\nDiscretize phi/psi into k=4-8 microstates (k by gap-heuristic on GT). Fit MSM at lag times tau in {0.1, 1, 10, 100} ps. Report t_2 implied timescale. Microstate assignment from GT only, then applied to generated.\n\n### 4.5 Hilbert amplitude and period\nMedian envelope amplitude and median period from zero-crossings. Sensitive to symmetric-signal vs rectified signal.\n\n### 4.6 Sanity \u2014 Cartesian and torsion RMSD\nPer-frame RMSD after Kabsch alignment (sanity; expected small since MDGEN operates in cartesian space; not informative for oscillation question). Torsion displacement RMSE (delta phi, delta psi, delta chi), absolute and circular.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Controls\n\n| Name | Definition | Recovers Preserved | Recovers Lost | Role |\n|------|------------|--------------------|---------------|------|\n| L0 constant-copy | gen = conditioning frame | No (zero ACF) | No | Floor |\n| L1 linear-in-atoms | Kabsch-aligned linear interp in atoms | Partially (slow trend) | No (no oscillation) | Non-negotiable beating baseline |\n| L2 linear-in-torsion | Linear in (phi,psi,chi), then atoms | Partially (sawtooth) | No | Stricter interpolation baseline |\n| L3 exact subsample passthrough | Input frames with interp | Trivially yes | No (zero power) | Upper bound on passive performance |\n\nInterpretation: L0 and L1 must fall below H1 by clear margin in Lost band; if L1 coincides with MDGEN, MDGEN is not oscillating at all (valid negative). L2 <= MDGEN establishes MDGEN beats straight-line torsion interp. L3 sets passive upper bound; zero score in Lost band by construction.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Statistical design\n\n- n = 32 independent generation seeds per (system, stride, torsion) cell.\n- 192 MDGEN generations total plus 128 control generations.\n- Independent seeds: MDGEN diffusion noise resampled; conditioning frames identical within cell.\n- 95 percent CIs on metric_1 and tau_c via BCa bootstrap over n=32 seeds.\n- Bonferroni-Holm correction across torsions per system; pre-declared effect-size threshold clears corrected alpha.\n- Code version, dataset checksum, seeds, and division among bands-of-interest locked before any aggregation.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Pre-registered decision rules\n\nA run is positive for H1 iff all hold under the strict primary reading:\n\n1. metric_1 in band: 95 percent CI contained in [0.5, 2.0].\n2. Beats L1 by margin: 95 percent CI strictly above L1's 95 percent CI with non-overlap.\n3. Beats L2: same non-overlap rule.\n4. Preserved-band sanity: 95 percent CI on metric_1 in preserved band within [0.7, 1.4].\n5. ACF consistency |tau_c_gen - tau_c_gt|/tau_c_gt <= 0.3 in preserved band.\n\nAny violation flips (system, S, torsion) result to negative. Overall verdict = modal sign across 6 cells, reported per system separately.\n\nFallback A: rule 1 becomes \"trend agreement at stride resolution (lowest 3 periods only).\" Fallback B: reduce to \"Ramachandran JSD <= 0.05 nats\" with stricter sample-size justification.\n\n---\n\n## 8. Failure modes and mitigations\n\n| Failure mode | Likelihood | Detection | Mitigation |\n|--------------|------------|-----------|------------|\n| MDGEN emits at dt_gen >> 1 ps; cannot represent libration | High | Inspect dt_gen; compute f_Nyq(dt_gen). If <= f_Nyq(S), Lost band empty -> Fallback A | Report under which S only trend-preservation test |\n| Topology mismatch (atoms renamed, ordering off) | Low-Med | mdtraj.Topology equality pre-check | Abort cell; report separately |\n| Insufficient GT length for Welch convergence | Med | Pre-flight segment count | Run more GT; cap reporting bandwidth |\n| Torsion segmentation ambiguity in chignolin | Med | Visual psi_i around suspected transitions | Pre-declared mask of well-defined residues |\n| Diffusion noise washes out generated | Med | PSD shape; flat-white-noise signature | Drop only if diffusion verifiably broken (cartesian RMSD > 3x threshold) |\n| Insufficient statistical power | Med (compute-dependent) | Bootstrap CI width | Drop chignolin before reducing n |\n| MDGEN non-convergence / explosion | Med | Generated std > 3x conditioning std | Discard seed; replace; cap replacement fraction |\n| JSD numerics from sparse bins | Low | Bins with <5 samples masked | Pre-declare \"minimum-bins-used\" |\n| Time-flat torsion distribution recovered but no oscillation | Expected | Direct inspection | Textbook Fallback-B-only positive |\n\n---\n\n## 9. Feasibility statement\n\nThis plan targets out-of-sandbox execution in a harness with:\n1. MDGEN diffusion module + checkpoint weights for bridging-frame variant.\n2. Python 3.x with mdtraj, numpy, scipy, matplotlib, and MSM tooling (PyEMMA or deeptime).\n3. GPU or CPU budget sufficient for 320 generations.\n4. Network off; all dataset code paths local.\n\nThis /workspace cannot run it: no MDGEN repo, no preinstalled Python deps, network disabled, GPU unavailable. Plan is design level only; runtime numbers are not included and will not be invented.\n\n---\n\n## 10. Out of scope\n\n- Cartesian free-energy landscape comparison. MDGEN is in cartesian space, so cartesian-FE agreement does not answer the torsion question.\n- Comparison to other generative-MD baselines.\n- MDGEN marginal stability / structure recovery beyond metrics listed.\n\n---\n\n## 11. One-paragraph summary\n\nTake fine-cadence ground-truth MD of alanine dipeptide (dt_truth ~ 100 fs, >= 10 ns) and chignolin (in-distribution). Construct subsampled conditioning at S in {1, 10, 100} ns. Run MDGEN (n=32 seeds/cell) to generate bridges. Compare torsion time-series (phi, psi; chi for chignolin) on (i) Welch PSD integrated power in lost band = primary, (ii) autocorr time tau_c, (iii) Ramachandran JSD, (iv) MSM implied timescales over lag-time sweep, plus Hilbert amplitude/period. Four pre-registered controls (L0 constant, L1 linear-atoms, L2 linear-torsion, L3 exact subsample) bound interpretation; H1 supported only when MDGEN metric_1 within GT 95 percent CI in lost band AND clears L1, L2 with non-overlapping CIs. If dt_gen precludes representation of lost band, default to Fallback A (trend preservation at stride resolution); if A unfeasible, Fallback B (marginals-only JSD). All thresholds, fallbacks, masks, and rules pre-registered before aggregation.", "evidence": "Inspected /workspace twice \u2014 contains only task.json (464 bytes). task.json / track.md explicitly states design-only with no required repos or compute. Environment notes confirm bubblewrap sandbox, network disabled, no preinstalled Python deps. Design grounded in (a) MDGEN's published bridging-frame training regime (~100 ns context spacing) which gives meaning to the lost-band framing of subsection 0.1, (b) standard MD torsion-analysis methodology (Welch PSD with mdtraj-extracted dihedrals, autocorrelation, MSM implied timescales via PyEMMA / deeptime), and (c) Welch convergence criterion (32 segments x 32 period-cycles -> ~18 percent estimator variance and usable 95 percent CI). No numerical result was computed; no runnable code was authored.", "assumptions": ["The strict reading (lost-band PSD recovery at fine cadence) is the intended success criterion; Fallbacks A and B are pre-declared weaker outcomes if the strict reading is structurally inaccessible under MDGEN's emitted frame cadence.", "MDGEN's generation regime targets bridging frames between two context frames tens to hundreds of nanoseconds apart; the per-frame interval of generated output dt_gen will be coarser than fs by design, which forces the strict reading to resolve around this fact via the lost-band intersection with f_Nyq(dt_gen).", "An MDGEN checkpoint bundled with the public release can be loaded with their inference script without additional fine-tuning for these systems.", "mdtraj can extract phi/psi/chi with identical atom-index conventions between MDGEN-generated and ground-truth structure files given matching residue numbering.", "Ground-truth fine-cadence data is available from public mdtraj / PyEMMA tutorial datasets for alanine dipeptide at a quality level sufficient for the chosen minimum-length criterion."], "uncertainties": ["The exact dt_gen of MDGEN's emitted frames is not stated in the public paper abstract and must be measured at run-time; if dt_gen ~= 5 ps or coarser, the lost band collapses and the strict reading is structurally unanswerable.", "Whether 32-segment x 32-cycle Welch gives a CI tight enough to discriminate the proposed H0 vs H1; a power calculation settleable only empirically.", "Whether sigma_phi and sigma_psi PSD distributions in alanine dipeptide under typical force fields have sharp enough features in the lost band to make the metric_1 factor-of-2 margin meaningful, or whether all signal of interest is sub-lost-band and the experiment reduces to a tight null.", "Choice of microstate count k for the MSM lag-time sweep (pre-registered as k=4-8 by gap-heuristic on ground truth) must be committed to before generation data is examined.", "Whether out-of-sandbox execution will be permitted at all; this design cannot be performed from /workspace due to dependency and network constraints, so this delivery is design only with no execution."]}", "origin": "completion"}, "llm_response_id": "chatcmpl-927a08d8-7724-4365-8670-1bbe9a3c22bf", "security_risk": "UNKNOWN", "kind": "ActionEvent", "source_event_index": 17}
